      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/FightInequality/status/1974348218432442471",
      "text": "✊🏾 WE, THE 99%\nThe People’s G20 Summit\n📅 20–22 November 2025\n📍 Constitution Hill, Johannesburg, South Africa\n\n🌍 Why We’re Rising\nWhile the G20 meets behind closed doors to serve the 1%, we — the 99% — will gather in Johannesburg to claim our power.\nThis is not a side event. It’s a direct counter-summit: a people’s space of resistance, solidarity, and action led by movements, workers, women, youth, and communities from across South Africa, Africa, and the Global South.\n\n✊🏿 What Justice Demands \n✅ Tax the 1% — make billionaires & corporations pay their fair share.\n✅ End Corruption — stop the theft of resources and invest in public services.\n✅ Drop the debt — build a fair deal that invests in people not banks.\n✅ Corporate Accountability — for environmental destruction, labour abuses and human rights violations. \n✅ Remake Multilateralism  — rebuild fair global institutions to serve people, not power.\n✅ Climate justice now — rich nations must pay their climate debt.\n✅ Value & redistribute care work — health, education & community first.\n✅ End Hunger — invest in local food production and people’s right to eat. \n\n🔥 Why Join\n↔️Our struggles are connected - we are reclaiming our collective imagination for a just world!\n🫶🏾Connect with movements from South Africa, the Global Majority & the world\n💪🏾Join groups to share ideas, organise, resist & build alternatives\n🎇Take part in a festival of justice, solidarity & culture\n\n🎶 Programme for the 3 Days of Power\nDay 1: Memory, Movements & Action\nStorytelling • Debates • Grassroots voices\nDay 2: Solutions Festival\nAlternatives • Artivism • Living libraries • Street actions\nDay 3: 99% Uprising Rally & Concert – celebrate each other and commit to the cause\n• Global artists • Cultural performances  • Launching Declaration\n\n🌐 Get Involved Now\n👉🏾👉🏾👉🏾 Visit https://t.co/aQmHng8Z4U \nOn the website you can:\n⏩Register to participate as an organisation or an individual activist.\n⏩Pledge solidarity and join working groups \n⏩Stay updated - and choose how we keep you informed.\n⏩Organise runway events, or link your existing event to the programme of action to build momentum towards November.\n\nFrom Soweto to São Paulo, Manila to Mombasa, Cairo to Kingston, we are organising, marching, teaching, dreaming, resisting!\n\n✨ Power to the People, Our Struggle is Now!\n \nWe are the 99%, and we are Rising.",
